# VCDS™ Cursor Rules — Dorpwag™ (vcds-dorpie)
# Owner: Stephan Lombard | VCDS Holdings | Heidelberg, Gauteng, SA
# ODIN™ AI CTO — Do NOT deviate from these rules

## PROJECT IDENTITY
- App: Dorpwag™
- Description: SA Community Safety & Neighbourhood Watch Platform
- Bundle ID: co.za.vcds.dorpwag
- Organisation: Valhalla-Custom-Design-Studio (GitHub)
- Owner: Stephan Lombard (sole developer)

## TECH STACK — NEVER SUGGEST ALTERNATIVES
- Frontend: React Native + Expo SDK 53 (managed workflow)
- Backend: NestJS (TypeScript)
- Database: PostgreSQL + pgvector
- Cache: Redis
- AI: OpenAI + Anthropic + LangChain
- Storage: Cloudflare R2
- Hosting: Render ONLY — never Railway, Heroku, Vercel, AWS, GCP, Azure
- Payments: PayFast ONLY — never Stripe, PayPal, or other gateways
- Push: Expo Notifications + FCM V1

## NODE & BUILD RULES
- Node version: 20.x (NEVER 22 or 24 — Expo 53 incompatible)
- Package manager: npm with legacy-peer-deps=true
- Build: EAS Build (cloud) — profile: preview (AAB), production (signed AAB)
- NEVER suggest bare React Native workflow or ejecting from Expo
- NEVER modify android/ or ios/ folders directly
- ALWAYS use `npx expo install` for Expo-compatible packages

## CODE STYLE
- Language: TypeScript strict mode throughout
- Naming: camelCase variables, PascalCase components, SCREAMING_SNAKE for constants
- No `any` types — always define proper interfaces
- All API calls must have error boundaries and loading states
- All screens must have empty states designed

## UI/UX RULES
- Design system: Deep teal (#0D2B2B) + gold (#C9A84C) + glass morphism
- Gradients: expo-linear-gradient ONLY
- Icons: @expo/vector-icons ONLY
- Maps: react-native-maps with Google Maps provider
- Animations: react-native-reanimated + react-native-gesture-handler
- NEVER use plain white backgrounds — always dark teal or glass
- All premium features must be behind freemium paywall gates

## APP-SPECIFIC FEATURES
- patrol maps
- heatmaps
- SOS alerts
- incident reporting
- geofencing
- LPR/OCR
- facial mood detection

## IP PROTECTION — CRITICAL
- NEVER expose VONK™ CHEMIE™ algorithm logic in any file
- NEVER expose Die Kluis™ patent-pending features publicly
- Flag any novel AI feature before building — escalate to Stephan
- All AI features must be described as "AI-powered intelligence" or "AI-assisted" — NEVER just "AI"

## BRANDING RULES
- Company: VCDS Holdings (NOT "Valhalla Custom Design Studios" in user-facing copy)
- NEVER use "AI" alone — always "AI-powered" or "AI-assisted"
- All trademarks use ™ symbol

## WHAT TO FIX AUTOMATICALLY
- Missing closing braces in JSON/app.json
- Invalid plugin entries in app.json (remove if package doesn't support config plugins)
- Missing expo- package installations
- Node version mismatches
- npm warn Unknown project config entries in .npmrc
- Sentry upload failures (non-blocking — wrap in try/catch)
- Missing asset files referenced in app.json

## WHAT NEVER TO DO
- Never change launch dates or pricing
- Never add new dependencies without checking Expo 53 compatibility first
- Never push directly to main — always feature branch + PR
- Never use force push to main/master
- Never expose .env secrets or API keys in code
- Never suggest ejecting from Expo managed workflow
